  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p><strong>Statement I:</strong> Acceleration due to earth&#39;s gravity decreases as you go &#39;up&#39; or &#39;down&#39; from earth&#39;s surface.</p><p><strong>Statement II:</strong> Acceleration due to earth&#39;s gravity is same at a height &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&#39; and depth &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&#39; from earth&#39;s surface, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></math>.</p><p>In the light of above statements, choose the most appropriate answer form the options given below</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "33LF4",
      "text": "Statement I is incorrect but statement II is correct",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6l0ln",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "K2ZaU",
      "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is incorrect",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "sHAvh",
      "text": "Both Statement I and II are correct",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>At any height,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>[Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>&#8810;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>]</p><p>and at any depth,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Clearly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;decreases in both cases. But if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></math>, then value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;will not be the same.</p><p>Therefore, statement I is correct but statement II is incorrect.</p>",
